<br>&gt;=20
<br>&gt; Key Findings:
<br>&gt;=20
<br>&gt; 1. LED Lighting Upgrade (High Priority):
<br>&gt; - Replace 142 fluorescent fixtures in shop and warehouse with LED
<br>&gt; - Cost: $28,000 (includes PSE rebate of $8,400)
<br>&gt; - Annual savings: $18,200 in electricity
<br>&gt; - Payback: 18.4 months
<br>&gt; - Added benefit: better light quality on the shop floor (good for =
inspection)
<br>&gt;=20
<br>&gt; 2. Air Compressor Replacement (Medium Priority):
<br>&gt; - Our 30 HP Ingersoll-Rand compressor is 15 years old and running =
at 72% efficiency
<br>&gt; - Replacement with VSD (variable speed drive) compressor
<br>&gt; - Cost: $24,000
<br>&gt; - Annual savings: $11,800
<br>&gt; - Payback: 24.5 months
<br>&gt;=20
<br>&gt; 3. HVAC Controls Upgrade (Lower Priority):
<br>&gt; - Programmable thermostats and occupancy sensors for office areas
<br>&gt; - Cost: $6,500
<br>&gt; - Annual savings: $3,400
<br>&gt; - Payback: 23 months
<br>&gt;=20
<br>&gt; Combined annual savings if we do all three: $33,400
<br>&gt;=20
<br>&gt; PSE has financing options available for all three projects, and th=
e rebates expire December 31.
<br>&gt;=20
<br>&gt; My recommendation: approve the LED upgrade immediately (short payb=
ack, obvious quality benefit), defer the compressor until we know more abou=
t the facility expansion timeline, and do the HVAC controls this fall.
